# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate the time evolution of the system with Pauli propagation {#simulate-the-time-evolution-of-the-system-with-pauli-propagation}"
msgstr "Simula la evolución temporal del sistema con propagación de Pauli {#simulate-the-time-evolution-of-the-system-with-pauli-propagation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we have our circuit, $U$, and observable, $O$, we can easily simulate the system in a few steps:\n"
msgstr "Una vez que tenemos nuestro circuito, $U$, y el observable, $O$, podemos simular el sistema fácilmente en unos pocos pasos:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Separate $U$, into its Clifford, $C$, and non-Clifford, $P$, parts such that $U=PC$ using ``evolve_through_cliffords``\n"
msgstr "Separa $U$ en su parte Clifford, $C$, y su parte no Clifford, $P$, de modo que $U=PC$, usando ``evolve_through_cliffords``\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagate $O$ through $P$, resulting in a new operator, $O^\\prime$, using ``pauli_prop.propagate_through_circuit``\n"
msgstr "Propaga $O$ a través de $P$, obteniendo un nuevo operador, $O^\\prime$, usando ``pauli_prop.propagate_through_circuit``\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evolve $O^\\prime$ through the Clifford part of the circuit using the Clifford evolution support built into Qiskit\n"
msgstr "Evoluciona $O^\\prime$ a través de la parte Clifford del circuito usando el soporte de evolución Clifford integrado en Qiskit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Approximate the expectation value as $\\langle0|O^\\prime|0\\rangle \\approx \\langle0|U^\\dagger OU|0\\rangle$ by summing the coefficients in $O^\\prime$ associated with fully-diagonal Pauli terms (Pauli terms containing either ``I`` or ``Z`` on all qubits). Remember, this is an approximation because we truncated terms from $O^\\prime$ as we propagated it through the non-Clifford part of the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Aproxima el valor esperado como $\\langle0|O^\\prime|0\\rangle \\approx \\langle0|U^\\dagger OU|0\\rangle$ sumando los coeficientes de $O^\\prime$ asociados con términos de Pauli totalmente diagonales (términos de Pauli que contienen ``I`` o ``Z`` en todos los qubits). Recuerda que se trata de una aproximación, porque truncamos términos de $O^\\prime$ al propagarlo a través de la parte no Clifford del circuito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As we run larger calculations, the expectation value approximations become more accurate. In this example, we saturate the full Pauli space at around $4^{10}\\approx10^6$, which is reflected in the curve flattening out between the final two points.\n"
msgstr "A medida que ejecutamos cálculos más grandes, las aproximaciones del valor esperado se vuelven más precisas. En este ejemplo saturamos todo el espacio de Pauli en torno a $4^{10}\\approx10^6$, lo cual se refleja en que la curva se aplana entre los dos últimos puntos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the plot below shows a monotonic convergence, Pauli propagation simulations do not generally converge monotonically. It is not unusual to see \"bumpy\" behavior in these types of plots.\n"
msgstr "Aunque el gráfico siguiente muestra una convergencia monótona, las simulaciones de propagación de Pauli en general no convergen de forma monótona. No es raro ver un comportamiento \"irregular\" en este tipo de gráficos.\n"

